      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oxidative tribolayer is self-healing.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer is the critical factor governing the superior wear resistance of HEA protective coatings.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::023::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting HEA coating has a complex, nanostructured microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The starting HEA coating can form an in situ tribolayer during wear.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::023::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The wear-generated tribolayer forms rapidly and is resistant to strain.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Oxidation and diffusion enabled by high compositional variety produce the tribolayer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10864269::web::015::wear_performance",
        "PMC11124323::web::023::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The full HEA's multielement chemistry accelerates diffusion-driven oxidation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical stress drives multielement surface rearrangement in the full HEA.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Accelerated oxidation and surface rearrangement quickly establish a protective tribolayer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::023::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing compositional complexity delays or inhibits tribolayer formation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Delayed or inhibited tribolayer formation results in less surface hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reducing compositional complexity results in higher wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10864269::web::015::wear_performance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The full HEA will form a tribolayer faster and more completely than the reduced-complexity variant.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The full HEA will exhibit greater surface-hardness evolution than the reduced-complexity variant.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The full HEA will have a significantly lower wear rate than the reduced-complexity variant.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10241162::web::011::remarkable_wear_resistance_and_wear_mech",
        "PMC10864269::web::015::wear_performance"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed relationship should hold across mechanical stresses and sliding speeds typical of coating wear applications in oxidizing environments.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Individual alloying elements may have dominant effects that cause deviations from the entropy-based trend.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11124323::web::023::4_1_element_analysis_of_wear_track",
        "PMC9267885::web::021::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
